  "recommendations_in_order": [
    "Keep1024site limit; review spatial failures and validate ranking at512vs1024 plus independent layouts before interpreting small optimizer gains.",
    "Remeasure16\u201332physically compatible previous points under fixed20mK/current objective, sites and random streams. Use same starting measurements and anchor for all methods; do not import old response values.",
    "Begin3\u20136well-supported sensitive properties or linked physical groups rather than17independent broad coordinates; open additional directions after observed improvement. Check C44 boundary as a physical model test before pushing it lower.",
    "Pilot likely expensive extreme points with small primary counts. Record cost/completion separately from J; add an improvement-per-time score weighted by measured completion probability, with no zero-loss substitute for a timeout.",
    "Compare GP/CMA/random/Sobol at common new-measurement counts20,40,60 and common elapsed time over at least3seeds, reporting initialization and failures separately.",
    "Allocate extra primaries/replicas to uncertain leaders and confirm2\u20133distinct finalists on1024sites and independent layouts with unused streams. Small-screening estimates can rank candidates but require bias checks.",
    "Only then test a small llm_bo arm against the identical GP without LLM. Keep same initial observations, model/site/seed inputs, measured trial count and elapsed-time accounting; credit LLM only for independently confirmed extra reduction."
